                "retweet_count": 6,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "More than 2,000 healthcare and support staff positions could go unfilled from VA regional healthcare networks in Pennsylvania.\n\nThe Coatesville VA Medical Center serves approximately 17,000 veterans in PA-06. When there is a staff shortage at the facility, it means fewer appointments, longer wait times, reduced mental health services, and less access to specialized care.\n\nWhen those jobs disappear, veterans are pushed into private systems that are often more expensive, less coordinated, and less responsive.\n\nThat is not reform. That is privatization by neglect. We are calling on the Trump administration to restore full staffing at our VAs.\n\nhttps://t.co/x3yMe9IeNp",
